From 91daeeb79ca07e5cb62a83dbceb76f43c0bfad7f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: harshanandak <harshanandak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 28 Jun 2026 12:31:46 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(shell): keep mobile sign-out reachable via single account
 control
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The bottom nav is the only account surface on mobile (the header is
hidden under 768px) and MonoProfile has no sign-out control, so a plain
/profile button would strand mobile users with no way to sign out.

Make the single account control the Clerk account button itself (the
sole sign-out / manage-account surface) via a BottomNavAccountCell that
renders the Clerk button once mounted and a /profile fallback button
while the Clerk chunk loads — exactly one interactive control at a time,
no invisible overlay.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
